From 0373e4171994d01a254187faa1400014338095dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] feat(video): run the d3d11 renderer on dxvk-native on
 linux

The NV2A renderer (nv2a_d3d11.c) and the framebuffer window were Windows
only. On Linux the renderer now builds against DXVK-native, which provides
d3d11/dxgi on Vulkan, with vkd3d-utils for D3DCompile, and the window is an
SDL2 window that DXVK's SDL2 WSI presents into.

- d3d11_posix.h: the few Win32 calls the renderer makes besides D3D, over
  pthreads; on x86-64, D3DCompile through vkd3d's ms_abi convention
- three HLSL tweaks vkd3d needs (isnan, a masked index,
  GetRenderTargetSampleCount only for pixel shaders)
- fb_present.c: SDL2 window thread with keys (as VK codes), mouse,
  focus, borderless fullscreen (F11, Alt+Enter, RECOMP_FULLSCREEN);
  closing it ends the process
- the device waits for the window, which brings SDL's video up
- CMake: XBOXRECOMP_DXVK (on by default, stub if DXVK, vkd3d-utils or
  SDL2 are missing); declare the kernel/video and nv2a/d3d8 link edges
  so GNU ld resolves them
- tests/d3d11_dxvk_posix: device, every shader and the window come up
